# fontkit, which pdfkit pulls in for font handling, reaches @swc/helpers — and
# @swc/helpers requires tslib at runtime without declaring it as a dependency.
# pnpm's isolated layout takes that declaration literally and the module is
# genuinely missing, so a PDF fails to compile with "Cannot find module tslib".
#
# packageExtensions in package.json states the missing dependency, but pnpm
# only acts on that when it builds the tree, so an existing install carries on
# without it. Hoisting tslib to the top-level node_modules puts it on the path
# every nested package walks up through, whatever the tree was built from.
public-hoist-pattern[]=tslib
